      "notes": "second seat on the same machine; the criteria were run, as stated here, and this is not an independent review: both seats are AI on one machine. Version 3 exists because version 2 could not pass as signed. A rehearsal of the real contractVerify of the owner's signed version 2 body, at a local commit holding only the leak scan exemption for its merge commit, as a non-root user on a Linux server with a fresh GitHub clone as the vault, failed the scope criterion on all seven tasks on scripts/leak-scan.mjs, and failed T1-c00. The T1-c00 cause the earlier rehearsals missed: contractVerify runs each criterion command with MEMEV_CONTRACT_BASE set to the base, and test/hooks-startup.test.mjs compared SR-1.29's start-up against that base, which already holds SR-1.29's change, so the ratio was about 1 against a 0.7 bar on every run. Their reruns did not set that variable, so the test was skipped and the failure was taken for a flake. A rerun now uses the verifier's environment, base included. Read against version 2: no criterion statement, verifier, requirement, stop rule or dependency changed; four paths are added to every task's scope, under reviewer note 3; the request gains one Version 3 paragraph and loses nothing. Run at PR 453 (the fixes under this version), as ci on the Linux server: the full suite without the variable, 1585 tests and 0 failures, with the SR-1.29 start-up test run, not skipped; with MEMEV_CONTRACT_BASE set to this contract's base, as the verifier sets it, the full suite again gives 1585 tests and 0 failures, the SR-1.29 tests included. The leak scan history is clean, a synthetic merge with GitHub's default subject is clean, and the same with no origin fails closed. For the verify: nothing else may land on memev main between PR 453 and the verify, since the scope range runs from the base to the verify head.",
